          "old": "So, King Belshazzar threw this massive party for a thousand of his honored ones. The wine was flowing like crazy. Belshazzar, feeling buzzed, randomly ordered the gold and silver cups that his dad, Nebuchadnezzar, had jacked from God's Temple in Jerusalem. He wanted to drink from them with his crew, his wives, and his side-chicks. When they brought out the fancy cups, the king, his boys, his wives, and his concubines all started drinking wine from them. They drank and drunkenly cheered for their own gods—idols made of gold, silver, bronze, iron, wood, and stone.",
